.TH KP-SYNC 1 "2026-10-28" "kp-sync 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kp-sync \- synchronize KeePass copies and manage access sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kp-sync
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR | \fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-ui\fR \fIMODE\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kp-sync
synchronizes KeePass database copies through a local hub, a version history,
and verified promotion or merge. Normal commands contact the per-profile
daemon. Use
.B \-\-no-daemon
for direct engine operations where supported.
.PP
The default configuration is
.IR ~/.config/kp-sync/config.toml .
The
.B \-\-profile
option loads
.IR ~/.config/kp-sync/NAME.toml .
The mutually exclusive
.B \-\-config
option selects an explicit TOML file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon [\-\-foreground] [\-\-debug]
Run the per-profile synchronization daemon.
.TP
.B run [\-\-raise-existing] [\-\-app NAME] [\-\- ARGS ...]
Synchronize, start or raise an application, and hold its lease.
An existing single instance is activated without pre-sync; a new instance
pre-syncs before launch. Drive-triggered
.B up
still synchronizes when an application is running.
.TP
.B up [\-\-drive-id ID] [MOUNTPOINT]
Attach an optional drive and start the default application.
.TP
.B attach [\-\-drive-id SERIAL:FS_UUID] MOUNTPOINT
Register and synchronize a removable drive.
.TP
.B detach [\-\-drive-id ID] [MOUNTPOINT]
Release a drive lease.
.TP
.B sync [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-no-daemon]
Synchronize configured copies, or classify them without writes with
.BR \-\-dry-run .
.TP
.B resolve
Retry pending user decisions.
.TP
.B eject
Perform a final synchronization and unmount the drive.
.TP
.B down [\-\-drive-id ID]
Detach a drive and, when configured and idle, stop the application and clean
runtime state.
.TP
.B drive-sync up|down \-\-mode main|secondary \-\-drive-id SERIAL:FS_UUID [MOUNTPOINT]
Submit a udevmon drive event to the daemon (up/down on the main laptop,
attach/detach otherwise) without waiting for synchronization. The rclone
credentials are provided separately and never touched.
.TP
.B session [\-w] [\-\-unconfined] USER@HOST[:PATH]
Open a foreground confined SSH/sshfs session to the staged database.
The optional
.B \-w
enables a read-write session.
.TP
.B service start|stop|status ssh-session|access-owner NAME
Manage a named SSH session or
.BR kp-access-owner .
Names are configured in
.BR kp-sync-config (5).
Managed services survive terminal closure and write logs to the systemd user
journal. Stopping an SSH session revokes its key and completes its post-sync.
.TP
.B service start|stop|restart|status daemon
Manage the installed default or selected profile daemon unit directly.
Start/restart verify control-socket readiness; status never activates it.
Status also reports each socket/path/timer's active and enabled state.
Stop leaves socket/path/timer activation enabled, so a trigger can restart
the daemon. Unsupported custom configuration mappings are rejected.
.TP
.B service enable|disable daemon [\-\-now]
Enable configured installed activation units, or disable all profile
socket/path/timer activation. Enable does not install or rewrite files.
Without \-\-now, running units are unchanged. With \-\-now, enable starts
triggers; disable stops triggers and idle-sync clients before gracefully
stopping the daemon. Explicit requests and desktop/udev launchers can still
start a disabled daemon; this is not masking or application suspension.
.TP
.B service uninstall daemon [\-\-desktop]
Disable and stop as above, then remove selected-profile generated unit files
and reload systemd. Keep shared templates, other profiles, drop-ins,
configuration, databases and runtime recovery data. Desktop entries are
removed only with \-\-desktop. Modified, unsafe or other-profile files are
refused; failures may leave partial progress. Avoid concurrent client requests.
.TP
.B access-op
Handle one authenticated kp-access file operation; intended as the
.B \-\-file-op-cmd
helper, not for interactive use.
.TP
.B restore [\-\-merge | \-\-replace] (--version SHA | --backup NAME | --file PATH) [--dry-run]
Restore older content, merging by default.
.TP
.B history
List retained database versions and current-boot backups.
.TP
.B retire-session [\-\-identity ID] [\-\-confirm ID]
Preview historical session identities, or retire one identity after exact
confirmation and runtime checks. Preview reads available shared history and
may contact configured baseline stores, but does not mutate history. Apply
requires
.B \-\-confirm
to exactly match
.BR \-\-identity .
Database copies are not deleted; deferred or failed publication is reported.
.TP
.B forget
Revoke this profile's cached passwords.
Does not disable a configured KeePassXC source or revoke its association.
.TP
.B keepassxc-disconnect
Remove local KeePassXC browser pairing for this host/profile without
contacting KeePassXC. Revoke the connection in KeePassXC to remove remote
authorization. A later interactive credential request may ask to pair again.
.TP
.B status [\-\-long] [\-\-json]
Show cached state in grouped persistent-copy and session blocks, with
recorded synchronization ages, leases, and pending decisions. Status does
not probe endpoints. Text hashes use at least 12 characters, extended to
distinguish recorded versions.
.B \-\-long
shows full hashes; JSON always preserves full hashes.
.TP
.B cleanup [\-\-store NAME | \-\-runtime] [\-\-apply] [\-\-confirm-writers-paused]
Preview obsolete bases in configured attached stores and the runtime cache,
or select one scope. Report candidate bytes, protected files, blockers and
partial errors as JSON. Apply requires an explicit scope. Shared apply also
requires confirmation that all other shared-history writers remain paused
throughout the operation, including other hosts and profiles.
The confirmation flag does not pause them automatically.
Only recognized base files absent from all available history are deleted;
retained versions and disconnected-copy ancestry remain protected.
History and database copies are never rewritten; base contents are not
downloaded for cleanup. Pending/recovery work or unavailable history blocks
apply. Cleanup bypasses automatic deletion batching. Local locks and remote
rechecks cannot replace the paused-writer requirement on Google Drive.
.TP
.B service install daemon [\-\-desktop]
Install or refresh selected-profile user units and required shared templates,
then reload systemd without enabling or starting units. Add desktop
menu/autostart entries only with \-\-desktop. Enable activation separately
with service enable daemon [\-\-now]. The old install-units command is removed.
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-self-test]
Check local integration and configured dependencies; some checks probe
external endpoints. The explicit self-test uses a temporary restricted
localhost SSH key and synthetic data.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the package version without loading configuration or contacting
services.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-ui " MODE"
Select
.BR auto ,
.BR tty ,
.BR gui ,
or
.BR none .
.TP
.B \-\-no-wait
Return after the daemon accepts a supported request.
.TP
.B \-\-no-daemon
Run supported synchronization operations in-process.
.TP
.B \-\-raise-existing
For
.BR run ,
raise an already-running KeePassXC window even when standard input is not a
terminal. A new instance is still started by the daemon.
.TP
.BI \-\-identity " ID"
For
.BR retire-session ,
select the exact session history identity to preview or retire.
.TP
.BI \-\-confirm " ID"
For
.BR retire-session ,
apply retirement only when this value exactly matches
.BR \-\-identity .
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show informational messages.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH NAMED SERVICES
Define SSH sessions with
.B [ssh_sessions.NAME]
tables and owner processes with
.B [access_owners.NAME]
tables in
.BR kp-sync-config (5).
For example:
.PP
.nf
[sessions]
enabled = true

[ssh_sessions.office]
target = "user@host:~/kp"
mode = "rw"

[access_owners.windows]
command = ["/path/to/venv/bin/kp-access-owner", "--config", "/path/to/owner.toml"]
.fi
.PP
Then use
.nf
kp-sync service start ssh-session office
kp-sync service status ssh-session office
kp-sync service stop ssh-session office
.fi
.PP
The same commands accept
.B access-owner
as the resource type. Service commands use systemd user services and do not
require an interactive terminal. The owner command is an argv array and is
never interpreted by a shell.
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
Install the Python package
.B argcomplete
(included as a kp-sync dependency), then add the appropriate command to the
shell startup file:
.PP
.nf
Bash: eval "$(register-python-argcomplete kp-sync)"
Zsh:  eval "$(register-python-argcomplete --shell zsh kp-sync)"
Fish: register-python-argcomplete --shell fish kp-sync | source
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully or a request was accepted.
.TP
.B 1
Operational failure; for
.B service status
this also means the named service is inactive.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
A synchronization decision is pending, or shared retirement publication is
unavailable or failed.
.TP
.B 4
One or more synchronization endpoints are unreachable.
.TP
.B 10
.B status
reports that synchronization would change something.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kp-sync/config.toml
Default configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kp-sync/NAME.toml
Named profile configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kp-sync/
Default profile's private runtime state. Named profiles use separate
runtime directories.
.SH HTML DOCUMENTATION
From a source checkout, install the optional docs extra in a separate Python
environment and run
.B python tools/docs.py build
for strict HTML generation, or
.B python tools/docs.py serve
for a loopback-only preview. See docs/contributing.rst for developer checks.
Documentation builds never activate profiles or contact endpoints.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kp-sync-config (5),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
